1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,290
We all know that cleaning our teeth is important, right?
我们都知道刷牙很重要，对吧？

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:10,830
Because, if you don’t clean them and things go wrong, they can cause you a lot of pain and discomfort.
因为如果不刷牙，牙齿出了问题，会给你带来极大的疼痛和不适。

3
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:19,310
We’re taught from a young age how to clean our teeth, but the question is – do we all clean our teeth in the same way?
我们从小就被教导如何刷牙，但问题是——每个人的刷牙方式都一样吗？

4
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:26,740
Is there a specific time, technique, or duration you should be incorporating into your dental routine?
在日常口腔护理中，是否需要遵循特定的时间、方法或是时长呢？

5
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:40,000
When our milk teeth first appear in our infant years, we are shown, often by our parents, how to clean them – a ritual normally accompanied by some kind of catchy song.
婴幼儿时期，乳牙刚长出来时，通常是父母手把手教我们刷牙——这个过程还常常伴着一首朗朗上口的儿歌。

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,100
As we mature, our baby teeth drop out, replaced by adult teeth.
随着我们长大成人，乳牙脱落，恒牙取而代之。

7
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:50,080
And soon it’s from trips to the dentists that we get more advice.
之后，我们从牙医那里得到更多关于刷牙的建议。

8
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:58,930
And that’s the issue – when trying to discover the best way to brush your teeth, it feels like there are so many different tips and tricks.
但问题也随之而来：当我们想找到最佳刷牙方式时，总会发现各种各样的技巧和窍门。

9
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:06,160
University College London (UCL) analysed 66 sources of toothbrushing advice from around the world.
伦敦大学学院分析了来自全球的66份刷牙建议资料。

10
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:13,540
The most commonly recommended techniques incorporated circular movements and horizontal brush strokes.
其中最常被推荐的刷牙方式是画圈和水平横刷。

11
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:25,580
However, there were some deviations. The angle of the brush, use of vertical movements and rigorous scrubbing were all variations on brushing advice.
不过，也存在一些不同的说法，牙刷的倾斜角度、竖刷的方式以及用力刷洗，这些都是刷牙建议中的不同版本。

12
00:01:25,580 --> 00:01:35,180
And it seems that not one single technique is the standard method – so, if that’s the case, how do we know if we’re doing it right?
看起来并没有哪一种方法是唯一的标准方式——既然如此，我们怎么判断自己的刷牙方式是否正确呢？

13
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:39,130
Well – there is some standard advice.
其实还是有一些标准建议的。

14
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:46,630
It seems that brushing for between two to three minutes, two or three times a day, is the best course of action.
每天刷牙两到三次，每次持续两到三分钟，这种做法是最稳妥的。

15
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:53,560
And if you’re one of these people who think it’s wise to brush straight after sugary foods to prevent decay, think again.
如果你觉得吃完甜食后立刻刷牙能预防蛀牙，那可就错了。

16
00:01:53,560 --> 00:02:02,190
Apparently, bacteria weaken the enamel almost immediately upon eating, so it’s wiser to wait for an hour or so before brushing.
很明显，吃完东西后，口腔内的细菌会迅速侵蚀牙釉质，所以最好等一个小时左右再刷牙。

17
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:15,120
So, while there is not one standardised technique, most dentists recommend a combination of horizontal and circular movements, lasting for between two to three minutes, two or three times a day.
因此，尽管没有统一的标准刷牙方法，但大多数牙医都建议结合水平横刷和画圈刷的方式，每天刷两到三次，每次两到三分钟。

18
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:18,920
Do that, and you might not need too many trips to the dentist.
坚持这样做，你去看牙医的次数或许就能少很多了。
